BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:alkazi-curatorial-research-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
SUMMARY:Deadline: Alkazi Foundation: Curatorial Research Fellowship 2027 (w
 ith CWIT and the V&A)
DESCRIPTION:A funded research residency (3rd edition of the Visiting Curato
 rial Research Fellowship) for mid-career cultural producers from India: ar
 tists\, scholars\, writers/editors and curators pursuing humanities-driven
  research in the V&A's global photography and visual-culture collections i
 n London. The awardee is announced in February 2027 and the fellowship sta
 rts April 2027.\n\nOrganisation: Alkazi Foundation for the Arts\, with the
  Charles Wallace India Trust and the Victoria and Albert Museum\nLocation:
  New Delhi\, India (organiser)\; the funded research residency takes place
  at the V&A Photography Section\, London. RESTRICTED: Indian citizens domi
 ciled in India\, aged 25 to 45\, mid-career.\nAward: GBP 1\,600 monthly st
 ipend for 3 to 6 months\, plus a GBP 800 contribution from CWIT towards in
 ternational return airfare\; visa expenses covered by the Alkazi Foundatio
 n. No application fee.\nDuration: 3 to 6 months\n\nMore: https://alkazifou
 ndation.org/call-for-entries-5/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_
 medium=referral
URL:https://alkazifoundation.org/call-for-entries-5/?utm_source=artificialn
 ouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:New Delhi\, India (organiser)\; the funded research residency take
 s place at the V&A Photography Section\, London. RESTRICTED: Indian citize
 ns domiciled in India\, aged 25 to 45\, mid-career.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tarbell-fellowship-2027-28@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261122
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:Deadline: Tarbell Fellowship 2027-28 (AI journalism)
DESCRIPTION:A year-long fellowship for journalists covering artificial inte
 lligence. Fellows complete a three-month full-time remote programme on AI 
 and journalism fundamentals\, attend a weeklong summit\, then work for nin
 e months as reporters embedded in a partner newsroom (current partners are
  in Hong Kong\, London\, Los Angeles\, New York\, San Francisco\, Seattle\
 , Washington DC and Cambridge).\n\nOrganisation: Tarbell Center for AI Jou
 rnalism\nLocation: Remote training\, then newsroom placement in the US\, U
 K or Hong Kong. In person.\nAward: USD 75\,000 to 120\,000 depending on ex
 perience and placement cost of living\; senior fellows (7+ years experienc
 e) USD 115\,000 to 135\,000. Summit travel and accommodation covered. No a
 pplication fee.\nDuration: 12 months: remote training 7 June to 6 August 2
 027\, in-person summit August 2027\, newsroom placement September 2027 to 
 May 2028 (extendable by one year).\n\nMore: https://www.tarbellcenter.org/
 fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.tarbellcenter.org/fellowship?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote training\, then newsroom placement in the US\, UK or Hong K
 ong. In person.
END:VEVENT
