SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 UTC: M+ Sigg Fellowship for Chinese Art Research 202
 6/27 (HKD 200\,000\, Hong Kong)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 30 Nov 2026 at 23:59 UTC.\n\nThe Sigg Fellowship for Chi
 nese Art Research supports new research on Chinese art in dialogue with th
 e M+ Collections\; the 2026/27 edition focuses on tradition and contempora
 ry Chinese art.\n\nOrganisation: M+\, West Kowloon Cultural District\nLoca
 tion: Hong Kong. Open to individuals or research groups of any nationality
 \; the fellowship depends on obtaining a Hong Kong visa.\nAward: HKD 200\,
 000 covering all expenses (travel\, living\, insurance and research costs)
 . No application fee mentioned.\nDuration: 3 to 6 months attached to M+ in
  Hong Kong.\n\nMore: https://www.mplus.org.hk/en/awards-and-fellowships/si
 gg-fellowship-for-chinese-art-research/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantd
 esk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.mplus.org.hk/en/awards-and-fellowships/sigg-fellowship-for-
 chinese-art-research/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=ref
 erral
LOCATION:Hong Kong. Open to individuals or research groups of any nationali
 ty\; the fellowship depends on obtaining a Hong Kong visa.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:parc-palestinian-research-fellowship-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github
 .io
DTSTAMP:20261104T151253Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261206
SUMMARY:Deadline: PARC Palestinian Research Fellowship 2027-2028 (up to USD
  6\,000\, arts\, humanities and social sciences)
DESCRIPTION:PARC's 28th annual fellowship competition for Palestinian schol
 ars funds field-based research in the arts\, humanities\, social sciences\
 , public health and environmental studies\; purely scientific research is 
 not eligible.\n\nOrganisation: Palestinian American Research Center (PARC)
 \nLocation: For Palestinian researchers regardless of residence or ID\; fi
 eldwork in Palestine\, Jordan\, Egypt or Lebanon.\nAward: Up to USD 6\,000
  per fellowship (tuition not covered). No application fee mentioned.\nDura
 tion: 2 to 12 months of fieldwork\; research to be completed by 31 Decembe
 r 2028.\n\nMore: https://www.parc-us-pal.org/fellowships-for-palestinians/
 ?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.parc-us-pal.org/fellowships-for-palestinians/?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:For Palestinian researchers regardless of residence or ID\; fieldw
 ork in Palestine\, Jordan\, Egypt or Lebanon.
END:VEVENT
